#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:314
msgid ""
"When using Create: Repackaged, place fluid gauges provided by this mod to "
"monitor and produce fluids. Fluids may be set in the <<figure-set-item,\"set "
"item\" screen>> by clicking the filter slot while holding a bucket of fluid "
"or by dragging a fluid entry from JEI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:316
msgid ""
"When using the other mods, regular factory gauges gain the ability to "
"monitor and produce fluids. Fluids may be set in the <<figure-set-item,\"set "
"item\" screen>> by right-clicking the filter slot while holding a bucket of "
"fluid or by dragging a fluid entry from JEI."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:318
msgid ""
"Fluids do not contain NBT data, therefore when monitoring a fluid, the "
"option to ignore NBT data disappears."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:320
msgid ""
"When using a fluid as an ingredient or output, scrolling on the ingredient "
"or output UI adjusts the amount by 1 B. Hold shift while scrolling to adjust "
"by 10 mB, or hold ctrl while scrolling to adjust by 1 mB. The output is "
"limited to 10 B per batch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:322
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ignore Item NBT Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: #ignore-data
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:325
msgid ""
"A factory gauge may be configured in the <<figure-set-item,\"set item\" "
"screen>> to ignore the NBT data of its <<term-monitored-item,monitored "
"item>>. When it is ignored, all items of the same type as the monitored item "
"are counted towards the <<term-storage-amount,storage amount>>, regardless "
"of their NBT data."
msgstr ""

#. type: #ignore-data
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:327
msgid ""
"Items with different NBT data do not stack. Therefore, when an <<term-"
"ingredient-gauge,ingredient gauge>> ignores NBT data, the consumer gauge may "
"receive the ingredient in more stacks than what appears in the <<term-"
"recipe,recipe>>. If the total number of items in a <<term-request,request>> "
"exceeds 9 stacks, the items are split into multiple packages."
msgstr ""

#. type: #ignore-data
#: ../src/factory-gauge.adoc:328
msgid ""
"If either <<crafting,mechanical crafting>> or <<arrange-ingredient,custom "
"arrangement>> is enabled, the behaviour is different. Each item stack "
"defined in the recipe must consist of items with identical NBT data. For a "
"unique set of NBT data possessed by N items in storage, items with this set "
"of NBT data are only sent if N is sufficient to fill one ingredient stack."
msgstr ""
